# fixedbugs, M-separate-compilation, 2026-08-25 (panel 092's queued half,
# the adjacent shape the sitting did not name).
#
# SYMPTOM: `-Werror=shorten-64-to-32` reads exactly what its name says, so
# `i64` against a header's `short` — and `i32` against `short`, and `i16`
# against `char` — converted in silence at exit 0, below the window the
# global flag watches. Measured the day panel 092's float repair landed:
# the same pragma mechanism was one flag short of the integer family too.
#
# CAUSE: clang files the sub-32 narrowings under -Wimplicit-int-conversion,
# which no global flag enabled — and enabling it globally would judge
# generated code, whose narrowings are deliberate casts.
#
# FIX: `-Wimplicit-int-conversion` is the fourth error inside the probe
# block's pragma. Its message text is the one NARROWED already matches
# ("implicit conversion loses integer precision"), so the mapper needed no
# new needle — only the pragma that makes it fire.
#
# `init_pair` is ncurses' own (short, short, short): a real header whose
# parameter is narrower than `int`, which is rare in C for the same reason
# this hole existed — default promotions make `short` parameters unusual.
#
# This file must NOT compile. It is built by the CLI surface test
# `an integer narrowing below the 64-to-32 window is the author's error`
# (suite_surface).

extern "curses.h" link "ncurses"
    function init_pair(pair: i64, f: i16, b: i16) -> i32    #~ ffi_parameter_type

function main()
    _ = init_pair(pair: 1, f: to_i16(2).must(), b: to_i16(3).must())
